# Simple smart answer

A simple smart answer uses a straightforward question-and-outcome tree without complex calculations. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/smart-answer/simple-smart-answer/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a small decision aid when a person needs to choose between a few guidance routes. Ask about something they can reasonably know, such as whether they want installation instructions or colour-setting guidance. Each outcome should lead to a clear next step.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep questions short, choices mutually understandable and an alternative for uncertainty. Preserve the chosen answer while reviewing the result. A simple decision can often be an ordinary list of links with explanatory text; do not add a wizard just to imitate a template.

## Home Assistant boundary

The examples use direct, working section links. They do not store answers or create a configuration. A more complex dependency graph belongs in a specified and tested implementation, not an expanding collection of ad hoc conditional markup.

